[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Angular Component Creation and Structure"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Angular components are the building blocks of Angular applications. Each component consists of three main parts: a template (HTML), a class (TypeScript), and metadata (the @Component decorator)."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Component Template (HTML)"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"The template defines the component's view. It's written in HTML and can include Angular-specific syntax for data binding, event handling, and structural directives."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"<!-- my-component.component.html -->
<div>
  <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
  <p>{{ message }}</p>
  <button (click)="handleClick()">Click me</button>
</div>"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"In this example, '{{ title }}' and '{{ message }}' are examples of interpolation, which displays data from the component's class. '(click)="handleClick()"' binds the button's click event to the 'handleClick()' method in the component's class."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Component Class (TypeScript)"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"The component class contains the logic and data for the component. It's written in TypeScript and defines properties and methods that the template can access."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"// my-component.component.ts
import { Component } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-my-component',
  templateUrl: './my-component.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./my-component.component.css']
})
export class MyComponent {
  title: string = 'My Component';
  message: string = 'Hello, Angular!';

  handleClick() {
    alert('Button clicked!');
  }
}"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"This class defines the 'title' and 'message' properties, which are bound to the template. The 'handleClick()' method is called when the button in the template is clicked."},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Component Metadata (@Component Decorator)"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"The '@Component' decorator provides metadata about the component to Angular. It tells Angular how to create and use the component."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'selector': The CSS selector that identifies the component in a template.  For example, '<app-my-component>'."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'templateUrl': The path to the component's HTML template file."},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'styleUrls': An array of paths to the component's CSS stylesheet files."},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"The '@Component' decorator is essential for Angular to recognize and manage the component."},{"order":17,"type":"subheading","text":"Creating a New Component using Angular CLI"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"The Angular CLI (Command Line Interface) simplifies component creation. Use the following command:"},{"order":19,"type":"code","text":"ng generate component my-new-component"},{"order":20,"type":"paragraph","text":"This command generates a new folder 'my-new-component' containing the component's TypeScript class, HTML template, and CSS stylesheet. It also automatically updates the 'app.module.ts' file to declare the new component."},{"order":21,"type":"subheading","text":"Component Structure Summary"},{"order":22,"type":"paragraph","text":"In summary, an Angular component is a combination of an HTML template for the view, a TypeScript class for the logic, and metadata provided by the '@Component' decorator. This structure allows for creating reusable and maintainable UI elements in Angular applications."}]
